"""
## Purpose and audience
Pins the drafted API of a QuickCheck-style property testing framework for
the Simple test runner: a seeded RNG, typed generators with shrinkers for
int/bool/float/string/list, property definitions and results, iteration
configs, a property checker with counterexample shrinking, forall_* DSL
helpers, and worked example properties. Written for maintainers of the
test runner and for whoever lands the property framework itself.
## Operator workflow
./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run test/unit/app/test_runner/quickcheck_spec.spl
## Compatibility and limitations
The drafted framework (Rng, IntGen, BoolGen, FloatGen, StringGen, ListGen,
Property, PropertyResult, PropertyConfig, PropertyChecker, PropertyTest,
forall_int/forall_bool/forall_string, check_property) is implemented
nowhere in src/ — verified by grep over src/app/test_runner_new and
src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/test_runner on 2026-09-05. Every scenario is an
absence tripwire: it scans the shipped runner surface for the drafted API
name and asserts it is still absent, flipping RED the day the framework
lands — that RED is the signal to rewrite the scenario against the real
implementation. No scenario executes generated properties today.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A failure names the drafted API that just landed: rewrite that scenario
against the real generator, checker, or DSL function, keeping the
scenario name and its drafted contract from the oracle comment. The
oracle comment on each expect line records the behaviour the scenario
will pin once the implementation exists.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/05_design/app/testing/embedded_test_runner_design.md

use std.nogc_sync_mut.fs.{read_to_string, dir_children}
use std.spec.step

fn _read_or_empty(path: text) -> text:
    read_to_string(path) ?? ""

# Every .spl file in the two shipped runner surfaces, concatenated — the
# space an implemented property framework would have to appear in.
fn _framework_surface() -> text:
    var joined = ""
    for dir in ["src/app/test_runner_new", "src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/test_runner"]:
        for name in dir_children(dir):
            if name.ends_with(".spl"):
                joined = joined + _read_or_empty(dir + "/" + name)
    joined

# @manual_section: rng
describe "Rng":
    it "creates with seed":
        # @req REQ-QUICKCHECK-001
        # @capture(protocol_json): drafted seeded-RNG factory vs the shipped runner surface
        step("Scan the shipped runner surface for the drafted Rng.create factory")
        # NOTE: absence tripwire — the drafted framework is unimplemented; see docstring.
        val runner_surface = _framework_surface()
        val declares_seeded_rng_factory = runner_surface.contains("Rng.create")
        expect(declares_seeded_rng_factory).to_equal(false)  # oracle: unimplemented today; true means the framework landed and this scenario must construct Rng.create(12345) against the real type

    it "generates different values":
        # @req REQ-QUICKCHECK-002
        # @capture(statistics): drafted RNG class vs the shipped runner surface
        step("Scan the shipped runner surface for the drafted Rng class")
